Not having a compose key in Windows annoyed me too, but there's a nice
workaround by the name of FreeCompose.
http://code.google.com/p/freecompose/
There's a slightly more annoying workaround: add the Spanish keyboard
layout. Doing so will give you the "acute accent modifier key" which will
cause the next letter to have an acute accent, if that letter supports it
(all vowels do, of course).

